  "theorem": "The nine tetracode history addresses form a primal translation subgroup P, but their delta-function basis span is not invariant under the null-history Laplacian. The canonical spectral object is instead the 3D coset-constant quotient with Fourier support P^perp. The order-three clock fixes P^perp pointwise at t*=2*pi/9, and its Maslov phases are 1,+i,-i. The tetracode C3 fixes these three dual modes pointwise. Adding one smallest nontrivial C3 orbit with Laplacian eigenvalue 6 contributes three omega modes, giving a minimal 6D C3-invariant sector containing both i and omega and hence all of mu_12."
